{"title":"2019 AIME II Problems/Problem 10","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>There is a unique angle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e8ed7a3ba22130ad3984eb2cd413406475a689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/5/465a8fb599a97128b9f411a55f6e19b801cf7ea5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/7/6a7dfa8a2a90d521b2b03f5b82a1fb9f85dce88c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$90^{\\circ}$\" width=\"24\" height=\"13\" /> such that for nonnegative integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/f/f7f922c121ea0412b836d0a5ad4ed130e03f4c20.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan{\\left(2^{n}\\theta\\right)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"69\" height=\"18\" /> is positive when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and negative otherwise. The degree measure of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e8ed7a3ba22130ad3984eb2cd413406475a689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/5/f650522cfc3d38eaa6a9a999cc47058c18d72a97.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac{p}{q}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -8px\" width=\"9\" height=\"21\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> are relatively prime integers. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/0/170200756543596efeb46fca1cf29a617e8c9192.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p+q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"41\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/7/567744e2ef4f7e63710dfcaa23fb8f836c352a9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan \\theta$\" width=\"38\" height=\"13\" /> is positive, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e8ed7a3ba22130ad3984eb2cd413406475a689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is in the first or third quadrant, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/e/e6e1820472e37e94dd2c0524e5252533447db6c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0^{\\circ} &lt; \\theta &lt; 90^{\\circ} \\pmod{180^{\\circ}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"196\" height=\"18\" />. \n</p><p>Furthermore, the only way <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/f/f7f922c121ea0412b836d0a5ad4ed130e03f4c20.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan{\\left(2^{n}\\theta\\right)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"69\" height=\"18\" /> can be positive for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> that are multiples of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is when:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/a/55a691f68e6d2b7767a739cf8553ac8db9aaeeb9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2^0\\theta \\equiv 2^3\\theta \\equiv 2^6\\theta \\equiv ... \\pmod{180^{\\circ}}.\\]\" width=\"275\" height=\"20\" />\n(This is because if it isn't the same value, the terminal angle will gradually shift from the first quadrant into different quadrants, making the condition for positive tan untrue. This must also be true in order for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e8ed7a3ba22130ad3984eb2cd413406475a689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to be unique.) \n</p><p>This is the case if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b19f3c88a5889a4020abf22946c287c411e80b76.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^3\\theta \\equiv 2^0\\theta \\pmod{180^{\\circ}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"175\" height=\"21\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/c/d9c641a085556de0e77e28e6a7d6674cee172b02.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7\\theta \\equiv 0^{\\circ} \\pmod{180^{\\circ}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"159\" height=\"20\" />. Therefore, recalling that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/8/578c6356882bd2793cf91ab4f6e344acfbcbe476.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0^{\\circ}&lt;\\theta&lt;90^{\\circ},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"107\" height=\"18\" /> the possible <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e8ed7a3ba22130ad3984eb2cd413406475a689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> are:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a5f993fbcaa60ae9c999ed47b66a1af68a14bca.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{180}{7}^{\\circ}, \\frac{360}{7}^{\\circ}, \\frac{540}{7}^{\\circ}.\\]\" width=\"134\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/f/a5f2b6f1f77704766ea7a1f2daeba97831153452.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{180}{7}^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"41\" height=\"40\" /> does not work since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/3/673acb2ec2dcfc705215f16273c619f9c3d35c63.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan\\left(2 \\cdot \\frac{180}{7}^{\\circ}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"118\" height=\"45\" /> is positive.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/b/b2bc71b33140a5a3af85c9581b0eb951668a91a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{360}{7}^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"37\" height=\"38\" /> does not work because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/e/f0e3b292925d64ecf321f9daf5a453146e0c0767.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan\\left(4 \\cdot \\frac{360}{7}^{\\circ}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"118\" height=\"45\" /> is positive.\n</p><p>Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/c/9ecf2e984251ef9877f7b031a0e5d819f10bc5d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta = \\frac{540}{7}^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"70\" height=\"38\" />, and a quick check verifies that it does work. Our desired answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/c/55ce38d820eb33f38748b69b2c07671ff1a99309.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$540 + 7 = \\boxed{547}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"122\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>As in the previous solution, we note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/7/567744e2ef4f7e63710dfcaa23fb8f836c352a9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan \\theta$\" width=\"38\" height=\"13\" /> is positive when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e8ed7a3ba22130ad3984eb2cd413406475a689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is in the first or third quadrant. In order for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/2/01235da5070fc0974e0cadf41ea8060d8b7bf244.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan\\left(2^n\\theta\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"69\" height=\"18\" /> to be positive for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, we must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e8ed7a3ba22130ad3984eb2cd413406475a689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/2/e92df436b16011d3aa9985885a8a6c3361ec9cfc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^3\\theta$\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/a/28ac0d59bd6bc31a11a57d99df386e9d0b6e077e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^6\\theta$\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" />, etc to lie in the first or third quadrants. We already know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/4/9e4bb9c1c0a62e48a19dd432ecd32244789f47ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta\\in(0,90)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"79\" height=\"18\" />. We can keep track of the range of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/0/920d783ddcc01fb050623632e3da54423f5d4ec3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^n\\theta$\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> for each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> by considering the portion in the desired quadrants, which gives \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/b/adb8bc70c7242125ba2d6e77d0d43d2be9db6b6b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[n=1 \\implies (90,180)\\]\" width=\"159\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/0/ad030a8550823eaac571c4c9cb69b9abecd9e03c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[n=2\\implies (270,360)\\]\" width=\"168\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/0/5c00dc18d3645522888ab2b69b2825855a927966.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[n=3 \\implies (180,270)\\]\" width=\"168\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/1/291e380e8502186972980b2114b8ab8340bf7e79.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[n=4 \\implies (90,180)\\]\" width=\"159\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/6/b462541fa0e978e5d3f3d7cc6dea6914bec7b314.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[n=5\\implies(270,360)\\]\" width=\"168\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/2/db2ebf711794f04b0d9d9a08c414a34bb71d2841.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[n=6 \\implies (180,270)\\]\" width=\"168\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/2/ce26e72ef1985f46ac9b2fedbe0879501540c94c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\cdots\\]\" width=\"18\" height=\"2\" />\nat which point we realize a pattern emerging. Specifically, the intervals repeat every <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> after <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/9/1d96ecc15129c5631ba4a2c6578e91e3d13e3baf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />. We can use these repeating intervals to determine the desired value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e8ed7a3ba22130ad3984eb2cd413406475a689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> since the upper and lower bounds will converge to such a value (since it is unique, as indicated in the problem). Let's keep track of the lower bound.\n</p><p>Initially, the lower bound is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> (at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/3/02349576cee613512cdf301a365f06c0760acab5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=0$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />), then increases to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/e/54ea8632a204c7436d1b9982407a517b8e02ee4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{90}{2}=45$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"64\" height=\"37\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/9/1d96ecc15129c5631ba4a2c6578e91e3d13e3baf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />. This then becomes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/d/6dde711000af2e48b377dc069cdff82de96f4543.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$45+\\frac{45}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"61\" height=\"37\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/b/6cb7ae00764b56ee2adf59e78a1ffde9685b80db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/d/6dde711000af2e48b377dc069cdff82de96f4543.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$45+\\frac{45}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"61\" height=\"37\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/3/5635737307f5f0651cced8ee2e6558a426fd27b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=3$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/a/51a760edbe285335e4245657b6030a002bc56c40.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$45+\\frac{45}{2}+\\frac{45}{2^3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"105\" height=\"37\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/c/39cf3e35a4981583288d2a7c4b34989916fb7360.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/7/1a76dc39bd9ff1a0f6b439266195d63b0cc97a1a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$45+\\frac{45}{2}+\\frac{45}{2^3}+\\frac{45}{2^4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"149\" height=\"37\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/e/84e75ddd39b9408f4d8e7fa62d2f6cdca00232de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />, etc. Due to the observed pattern of the intervals, the lower bound follows a partial geometric series. Hence, as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> approaches infinity, the lower bound converges to \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/4/d64a015a234ce88413faa1dcad763698614329b6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{k=0}^{\\infty}\\left(45+\\frac{45}{2}\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\frac{1}{8}\\right)^k=\\frac{45+\\frac{45}{2}}{1-\\frac{1}{8}}=\\frac{\\frac{135}{2}}{\\frac{7}{8}}=\\frac{540}{7}\\implies p+q=540+7=\\boxed{547}\\]\" width=\"582\" height=\"50\" />-ktong\n</p><p><b>Extra note:</b> If you are still unsure, you can check the upper bound to see if the top converges. This value comes out to be: \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/b/e9b1c8ca624c55108ce729a351f0c2abd45e8957.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$90-\\frac{90}{2^3}-\\frac{90}{2^6}-\\cdots=90\\left(1-\\sum_{k=1}^{\\infty}\\frac{1}{2^{3k}}\\right)=90\\left(1-\\frac{1}{7}\\right)=\\frac{540}{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"485\" height=\"56\" />.\n</p><p>Thus, the limit does in fact converge to the same value on both sides. ~eevee9406\n</p><p><b>Extra extra note:</b>\nThe top bound is arguably easier to prove because there are less terms added -dragoon\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/3/7f3c703e7c9bf7c86ba7d4569639b10cda6c2aba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan\\left(\\theta\\right) &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"88\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/f/e0fba87ee0dbac4f781c4ae80591cd1ebdb367c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 &lt; \\theta &lt; 90$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"84\" height=\"13\" />.  Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/a/9ea5e9cb21023122d9d6b255027f4622250d5161.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan\\left(2\\theta\\right) &lt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"97\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e8ed7a3ba22130ad3984eb2cd413406475a689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> has to be in the second half of the interval (0, 90) ie (45, 90).  Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/2/ee29bbb1c9c986c0dfe43958a76b8c581604b528.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan\\left(4\\theta\\right) &lt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"97\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e8ed7a3ba22130ad3984eb2cd413406475a689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> has to be in the second half of that interval ie (67.5, 90).  And since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/4/25470368106879baa09b701a38ac385d36a2aca1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan\\left(8\\theta\\right) &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"97\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e8ed7a3ba22130ad3984eb2cd413406475a689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> has to be in the first half of (67.5, 90).  Inductively, the pattern repeats: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e8ed7a3ba22130ad3984eb2cd413406475a689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is in the second half of the second half of the first half of the second half of the second half... of the interval (0, 90).  Consider the binary representation of numbers in the interval (0, 1).  Numbers in the first half of the interval start with 0.0... and numbers in the second half start with 0.1... .  Similarly, numbers in the second half of the second half start with 0.11... etc.  So if we want a number in the first half of the second half of the second half... of the interval, we want its binary representation to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/e/9ee19357b142a1098f776dda7915eb1ab86a64fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.11011011011..._2 = \\frac{6}{7}_{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"186\" height=\"38\" />.  So we want the number which is 6/7 of the way through the interval (0, 90) so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/9/6c9181b5bdb966b06768d64b9d0367f0e05880f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta = \\frac{6}{7}\\cdot 90 = \\frac{540}{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"131\" height=\"37\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/8/678861cf29ca8e3deeb18ac8a40d132f0544211e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p+q = 540 + 7 = \\boxed{547}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"187\" height=\"23\" />\n</p><p>~minor edit by <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mathkiddie\" title=\"Mathkiddie\">Mathkiddie</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>With some simple arithmetic and guess and check, we can set the lower bound and upper bounds for the \"first round of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> powers of two\", which are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/a/57ac838af161b181b2992784a623691eeb7a5bec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{540}{8} = 67.5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"87\" height=\"37\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/b/38bcf7e80ce7f2339289514d50d903e8bb647513.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{630}{8} = 78.75$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"96\" height=\"37\" />. Going on to the \"second round of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> powers of two, we set the new lower and upper bounds as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/a/c5a1b36154ef59ddf8bb1e623f9b46d357145ae8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{360 \\times 12.5}{64} = 70.3125$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"168\" height=\"38\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/7/f675a998ab6c01fe40eb58a4bed8ad0cf85a1529.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{360 \\times 13.75}{64} = 77.34375$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"186\" height=\"38\" /> using some guess and check and bashing. Now, it is obvious that the bounds for the \"zeroth round of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> powers of two\" are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/c/bfcfee7bd8a5e15e5f6b7881c138de43651572a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$90$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, and notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/9/809d555a35866f092b8281f909d2978fd8231cf3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$90 - 78.75 = 11.25$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"146\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/8/fd857664f84db3e7520ac45d06fca15974387807.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$78.75 - 77.34375 = 1.40625$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"215\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/a/9ba19f10f58f71e48cdb41cb76cbe4d10405207e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{11.25}{1.40625} = 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"96\" height=\"38\" />.\nThis is obviously a geometric series, so setting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/7/c67dcc2fabdc566526c4dd855472299181f9af06.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11.25$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"40\" height=\"13\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/d/9ad99798ec4c38e165cf517cb9e02b1c9e824103.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, we obtain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/b/8db2dfa798e533eaf4f1a22cde0afd22d90207e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$90 - (u + \\frac{u}{8} + \\frac{u}{64} + ...)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"181\" height=\"33\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/8/1d81d8fa6b4463071e955b6ac358701df3043c2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$90 - \\frac{u}{1-\\frac{1}{8}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"84\" height=\"39\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/7/0a7e73700697b607b069588dc0719d1f90236647.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{u}{\\frac{7}{8}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"16\" height=\"41\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/4/bc4699faca987b28d6f7884dac0bfb64d8a48272.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{45}{4} \\times \\frac{8}{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"56\" height=\"38\" /> which simplifies to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/4/9c47d845856c8900793f72ff24c4816a5834eec9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{90}{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" />. We can now finally subtract <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/4/9c47d845856c8900793f72ff24c4816a5834eec9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{90}{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" /> from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0611ec68564d67ed79ba724f2b35bbc555c92b8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{630}{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"29\" height=\"37\" /> and then we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/4/874c0b836cd5848ae104cc84badbbff6f33ebc91.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{540}{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"29\" height=\"37\" /> as the unique angle, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/e/92e700a60eb682c433db59300195552dfd7b4a94.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{547}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"40\" height=\"25\" /> is our answer.\n-fidgetboss_4000\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5\">Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is the only number n such that f(x) = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/6/a16fbbb6b271f4d9663045c4bcc9ef2209667680.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{\\lfloor x\\rfloor}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/d/5ed96591f1a6c4291d14b92a1290379a01122555.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(mod 7)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"60\" height=\"18\" />  has a period of 3, we find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e8ed7a3ba22130ad3984eb2cd413406475a689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/e/14e21580231bf91fe33de0ae763dfe178433dddb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${\\frac{180}{7}}^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"41\" height=\"40\" />. Note that the tangents of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/e/14e21580231bf91fe33de0ae763dfe178433dddb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${\\frac{180}{7}}^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"41\" height=\"40\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/5/d8527733a37171c0e99c04c82c1be19fb0817eb7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${\\frac{360}{7}}^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"41\" height=\"40\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/e/8aed10083c4729cd20bc6436b714df7264c10951.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${\\frac{540}{7}}^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"41\" height=\"40\" /> are positive while those of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/1/bb116dca3f05f4fb04a338029444675cf5d1c9e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${\\frac{720}{7}}^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"41\" height=\"40\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/a/10a7dcffb1f713b026f71cd72c1a5083a03fa19c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${\\frac{900}{7}}^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"41\" height=\"40\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/9/3e9a50ac2c65324770a12d09fb25c888c586dd98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${\\frac{1080}{7}}^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"50\" height=\"40\" /> are negative. With a bit of trial and error, we find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e8ed7a3ba22130ad3984eb2cd413406475a689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/e/8aed10083c4729cd20bc6436b714df7264c10951.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${\\frac{540}{7}}^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"41\" height=\"40\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/2/5625b9a365743f90c5b6ffea94070ec38d57e76c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$540+7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"60\" height=\"15\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/e/92e700a60eb682c433db59300195552dfd7b4a94.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{547}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"40\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~ <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=User:Afly\" title=\"User:Afly\">Afly</a> (<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=User_talk:Afly&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"User talk:Afly (page does not exist)\">talk</a>)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AIME_II\" title=\"2019 AIME II\">2019 AIME II</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AIME_II_Problems\" title=\"2019 AIME II Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AIME_II_Answer_Key\" title=\"2019 AIME II Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2019\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2019 AIME II Problems/Problem 9\">Problem 9</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2019 AIME II Problems/Problem 11\">Problem 11</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2019 AIME II Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2019 AIME II Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2019 AIME II Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2019 AIME II Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2019 AIME II Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2019 AIME II Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2019 AIME II Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2019 AIME II Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2019 AIME II Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2019 AIME II Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2019 AIME II Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2019 AIME II Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2019 AIME II Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2019 AIME II Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017055432\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.056 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.076 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 675/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1808/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 130/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 21762/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.491      1 -total\n 58.72%    7.335      1 Template:AIME_box\n 39.53%    4.938      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:17420:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017055432 and revision id 272687. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}